GRUB theme of the install ISO's boot menu ("quoth"), installed by
cauldron_iso_bootloader to boot/grub/themes/smgl with the unicode.pf2 font
from the build chroot's grub2. Without the font GRUB keeps its text menu.

bg.png      1440x1440, black, with SMGL's Quoth crow (Quoth.svg, the team's
            artwork) inverted to a grey-to-white gradient, 28% of the image
            height, centred at 22%. The theme scales it to the screen height
            ("fitheight"), so the crow grows with the screen and keeps its
            shape; the menu is placed in percentages of the height below it.
            (An image component would be stretched: GRUB scales its width
            and height separately, and never below the file's own size.)
menu_*.png  the menu box: #161616 with a dark-red (#781414) border
select_*.png the selected entry: #5f1010

Checked in QEMU (OVMF, GRUB 2.12) at 1024x768, 1920x1080 and 1200x1920.
GRUB 2.12 doesn't draw 4-bit palette PNGs: keep the images 8-bit RGB(A).
